1
00:00:00,256 --> 00:00:01,907
We call all of it “the AI,”

2
00:00:01,990 --> 00:00:03,310
but it's three layers:

3
00:00:03,358 --> 00:00:04,430
can you tell them apart?

4
00:00:04,856 --> 00:00:07,240
The model, the capability that predicts and

5
00:00:07,250 --> 00:00:10,471
generates; the agent, the entity that perceives,

6
00:00:10,481 --> 00:00:13,325
decides and acts; the harness, the system

7
00:00:13,335 --> 00:00:15,257
that connects context and tools.

8
00:00:15,660 --> 00:00:16,308
Case one:

9
00:00:16,545 --> 00:00:18,622
Codex gets a task, edits files and

10
00:00:18,632 --> 00:00:20,235
runs tests until it's done.

11
00:00:21,164 --> 00:00:21,706
Agent:

12
00:00:21,895 --> 00:00:24,385
there's a goal, decisions and actions, and

13
00:00:24,395 --> 00:00:26,459
it uses a model inside a harness.

14
00:00:26,868 --> 00:00:29,559
A layer limits permissions, logs traces and

15
00:00:29,569 --> 00:00:31,608
cuts off high-impact actions.

16
00:00:32,552 --> 00:00:33,129
Harness:

17
00:00:33,307 --> 00:00:34,700
it governs how the model or the

18
00:00:34,710 --> 00:00:35,889
agent is used.

19
00:00:36,300 --> 00:00:38,731
Claude Sonnet with no memory, no tools

20
00:00:38,741 --> 00:00:39,885
and no outer loop.

21
00:00:40,832 --> 00:00:41,362
Model:

22
00:00:41,528 --> 00:00:43,027
with nothing that lets it act, it's

23
00:00:43,037 --> 00:00:44,228
still just a model.

24
00:00:44,628 --> 00:00:47,000
So when something fails or improves, don't

25
00:00:47,010 --> 00:00:49,616
blame or praise “the AI.” Ask:

26
00:00:49,664 --> 00:00:51,373
model, agent or harness?

27
00:00:51,808 --> 00:00:54,107
Three layers, three responsibilities.

28
00:00:54,524 --> 00:00:56,036
Save it, and share it with someone

29
00:00:56,046 --> 00:00:58,003
who still calls it all “the AI.”

